AHS-020 — Deployment Architecture

Document ID: AHS-020
Title: Deployment Architecture
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

Architectural Views: Deployment, Implementation, Logical

1. Purpose

This specification defines the canonical Deployment Architecture of the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Deployment Architecture establishes how Atlas components, services, data, and communications are realized across physical and virtual environments while preserving the canonical cognitive architecture and implementation independence.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Deployment principles
Deployment units
Execution environments
Topologies
Scalability
Resilience
Availability
Operational governance

This specification does not mandate cloud providers, operating systems, container platforms, orchestration tools, or infrastructure technologies.

3. Canonical Definition

Deployment Architecture is the implementation-independent realization of the Atlas architecture across one or more execution environments while preserving canonical semantics, interoperability, security, and governance.

4. Deployment Objectives

Atlas deployments SHALL:

Preserve canonical architecture.
Preserve engineering semantics.
Support scalability.
Support resilience.
Support high availability.
Support observability.
Support portability.
Remain technology independent.
5. Deployment Principles

Every Atlas deployment SHALL follow these principles.

Architecture Preservation

Deployment SHALL NOT alter the canonical architecture.

Technology Independence

Deployment SHALL remain independent of specific infrastructure products.

Loose Coupling

Deployment units SHALL communicate through canonical interfaces.

Independent Scalability

Components MAY scale independently.

Fault Isolation

Failures SHALL remain isolated where practical.

Operational Observability

Deployments SHALL expose sufficient telemetry for monitoring and diagnostics.

Automation First

Deployment SHOULD support automated provisioning, configuration, and lifecycle management.

