7. Deployment Topologies

Atlas supports multiple deployment topologies.

Standalone

Single-node deployment for development, testing, or small projects.

Client–Server

Centralized services supporting multiple clients.

Distributed

Services execute across multiple nodes.

Cloud Native

Containerized, elastic deployment.

Hybrid

Combination of cloud, on-premises, and edge environments.

Edge

Localized execution near engineering assets or IoT devices.

Federated

Multiple independent Atlas deployments collaborating through standardized interfaces.

8. Execution Environments

Atlas MAY execute within:

Local workstation
Enterprise server
Private cloud
Public cloud
Hybrid cloud
Edge computing platform
High-performance computing cluster
Digital Twin infrastructure

Execution environments SHALL remain transparent to the cognitive architecture.

9. Scalability Model

Atlas SHALL support:

Horizontal Scaling

Additional service instances.

Vertical Scaling

Additional resources per instance.

Functional Scaling

Deployment of new capabilities without architectural redesign.

Geographic Scaling

Deployment across multiple regions while preserving canonical communication semantics.

10. Resilience Model

Deployments SHALL support:

Failure isolation
Service recovery
Retry mechanisms
Graceful degradation
Redundancy
Backup
Disaster recovery

Resilience SHALL preserve engineering integrity.

11. Availability Model

Atlas deployments SHALL define:

Availability objectives
Recovery objectives
Maintenance procedures
Health monitoring
Capacity planning

Availability requirements SHALL be documented.

12. Operational Observability

Deployments SHALL provide:

Metrics
Logs
Traces
Health status
Performance indicators
Capacity information
Alerting

Observability SHALL support operational governance and engineering traceability.

